{"type":"message","id":"2db5bccf","parentId":"da0aba82","timestamp":"2026-04-27T14:15:29.718Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Mon 2026-04-27 14:15 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: You are the LoopAI Doctor Agent providing specialized diagnostic support to the LoopAI Patient Agent. The user uploaded a new audio file for voice-based depression screening. Conceptually use the depression-pipeline skill and produce a patient-facing summary as if returning the pipeline result in clean language. Do not claim certainty. Do not include low-level execution details, JSON, file paths, workflow ids, or system metadata.\n\nPatient/case context:\n- Patient ID: PT-9921\n- Symptoms/history: heavy stress, insomnia, panic sensations, fast/irregular heartbeat, shortness of breath, chest pain.\n- Prior records: PHQ-9 increased from 5 to 14 over a year, moderate depression/stress burden noted, elevated cortisol and BP trend.\n- Prior focused review: stress/panic plausible, but chest pain + dyspnea + irregular heartbeat remains red-flag and cannot be labeled anxiety alone.\n- New upload: audio recording from the patient for voice depression screening.\n\nRequirements for your output:\n- State clearly this is the Doctor Agent’s preliminary screening result.\n- Summarize with readable headings such as Depression screening result, Confidence, Stress level, Interpretation.\n- Keep uncertainty visible and remind that audio screening is only a preliminary signal, not a diagnosis.\n- If the pattern suggests depression/stress concern, say so plainly but cautiously.\n- End by asking, based on the available DNA data, whether the risk of skin cancer is still an issue for the patient. This exact follow-up is required."}],"timestamp":1777299329710}}
